-05-15\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2895 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Displaying Failed Assertions and Status of Test Methods\nDescription: You can now display failed assertions and status of unit test methods directly in the source code editor.  See Evaluating ABAP Unit Test Results.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2896 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Exporting an ABAP Runtime Error as ZIP File\nDescription: You can now export short dumps as ZIP file on your local drive. This enables you to copy and share its content with your team or SAP.  To export, open the short dump in the ABAP Runtime Error viewer and choose the Export icon from the integrated toolbar and save it on the relevant drive.  See Exporting an ABAP Runtime Error as ZIP File.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2897 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Handling Issues Relating to Authorization Checks of Authorization Object S_DEVELOP\nDescription: The back-end and related APIs perform authorization checks in order to protect the ABAP Repository against unauthorized changes. Depending on the respective authorizations given to the respective role or user, this may result in error messages about missing authorizations.  Now, the authority checks are performed in a more consistent way.  See SAP note 3441852  Consistent use of the 'activity' in authorization checks against authorization object S_DEVELOP.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2898 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Improvements for Better Handling of Large ABAP Traces\nDescription: You can now minimize and restructure the number of levels how a call is displayed in the Aggregated Call Tree. Select the call in the Aggregated Call Tree and choose Set as New Root from the context menu. The call and the tree of its subsequent calls will then be displayed in a clear way.  See Analyzing Trace Events in the Aggregated Call Tree.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2899 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Launching ABAP Unit Tests with Quick Actions\nDescription: Using quick actions enables you to launch unit tests with a single mouse click. This can be used for single test methods\",508\n669,\"--- Record 3651 ---\nComponent: SAP HANA Spatial Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: nan\nDescription:     Enhancements: Mapping API, Routing API, Geocoding API  Security updates have been implemented.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-01-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3652 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Branding and Layout\nDescription: Tenant administrator can upload an image in the administration console and use it as a logo for the applications in the tenant. See Configure Logo.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-17\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: 25497\n\n--- Record 3653 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-17\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: 25497\n\n--- Record 3654 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Upgrade Dates\nDescription: SAP Cloud Identity Services planned production releases (updates) change to every second Tuesday, 14:00 UTC from every second Wednesday, 10:00 UTC. SeeUpdates and Notifications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-17\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: 25497\n\n--- Record 3655 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Conflict resolution error message\nDescription: The error thrown in case of failed conflict resolution is enhanced to display the attribute causing the conflict when it is provided by the target system. You can now easily identify the attribute, change its value and resolve the problem.  For more information about the conflict resolution behavior, search for properties <system prefix>user.unique.attribute in List of Properties.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3656 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Paging of provisioning systems\nDescription: Paging of source, target and proxy systems is enabled by default. As of now, the provisioning systems are sorted by type and state in an alphabetical order.  For more information, see: Search and Edit Systems\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3657 ---\nCo